  "refinements": [
    "Seven actual caller families distinguish native release wait from managed condvar queue and root/control effects",
    "WaitContext/WaitFrame/WakeLease supply owned scratch, capacity, OS-handle borrow, wake identity/predicate and declared time/signal/affinity policy",
    "Acceptance commit transfers resource release authority and owned task record; failed notification, interrupted response and cancelled observer do not discard accepted custody",
    "Cooperative cancellation preserves close stage and payload/external-effect disposition; no arbitrary thread-kill or destructive-call replay guarantee",
    "Eight shutdown obligations close root issuers but count authorized descendants, drain actual work/readers/retained dependencies, then stop/join and release wait/library/code resources",
    "Old implicit-wait device_cleanup and error/free group body cannot remain opaque migrated authorities; qualified close/release leaves are bounded reuse",
    "Twelve matched support families, concrete C failure-funnel versus Zig lexical builder, six change events, five retirement conditions and seven net-benefit/refutation rows retain unresolved bounds"
  ],
